n\n3. **Calculate the degree of the product \\( p(t) \\cdot q(t) \\):**\n   - The degree of \\( p(t) \\) is 7.\n   - The degree of \\( q(t) \\) is 7.\n   - Therefore, the degree of the product \\( p(t) \\cdot q(t) \\) is:\n     \\[\n     7 + 7 = 14\n     \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The degree of \\( p(t) \\cdot q(t) \\) is 14.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{14}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{14}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:327"}
